---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeadMagnetForm from '../components/LeadMagnetForm.astro';

const title = "The Long Road — The Geriatrician's Guide";
const description = "A 200-page guide to senior living decisions written by a Stanford-trained geriatrician. $97. 30-day guarantee.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="wrap section">

    <p class="eyebrow">Flagship Guide</p>
    <h1 class="product-hero__title">The Long Road</h1>
    <p class="product-hero__sub">Senior living decisions from first signs of decline through end-of-life. Written by a geriatrician.</p>
    <p class="product-hero__price">$97</p>
    <!-- LEMON SQUEEZY PRODUCT URL HERE -->
    <a class="btn btn--accent" href="#">Get Instant Access &mdash; $97
      <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </a>
    <p class="guarantee">30-day money-back guarantee. No questions asked.</p>

    <h2 class="section-head" style="margin-top:56px">What&rsquo;s inside</h2>
    <ul class="whats-inside">
      <li>The contract red flags that cost families the most &mdash; arbitration clauses, level-of-care upcharges, and the 30-day notice trap.</li>
      <li>How senior living actually prices: base rent vs. care tiers, and the line items that quietly double a monthly bill.</li>
      <li>How to evaluate a memory care unit clinically &mdash; staffing ratios at night, elopement protocols, and what a locked door does and doesn&rsquo;t mean.</li>
      <li>Polypharmacy and medication risk: the five-or-more-medications threshold and how to get a real medication review before a move.</li>
      <li>Conversation scripts &mdash; what to say to a parent who refuses to discuss it, and to a sibling who disagrees.</li>
      <li>The questions to ask on a tour, in order, with the answers that should make you walk away.</li>
      <li>Planning before the crisis: the documents, the money math, and the timeline that keeps a fall from forcing a rushed decision.</li>
      <li>End-of-life and the transition to hospice &mdash; what to expect, and how to advocate when your parent no longer can.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="free-chapter" style="margin-top:48px">
      <p>Not sure yet? Read a free chapter before you buy.</p>
      <!-- FREE CHAPTER LINK HERE -->
      <a class="textlink" href="#" style="color:var(--golden);border-color:var(--golden)">Read the Free Chapter
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="disclaimer"><em>The information in this book is for general educational purposes only. It does not constitute medical advice, financial advice, or legal advice, and reading this book does not create a physician-patient relationship. Clinical decisions should be made in consultation with the person&rsquo;s treating healthcare team. Financial and legal decisions should be made with qualified professionals.</em></p>

  </div>

  <LeadMagnetForm label="Not ready for the book? Start with the free checklist." />

</BaseLayout>
